<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">A necessary optical subtlety</p>
    <h2 id="t-polarity">Polarity Is Not One Binary Switch</h2>
    <p>Light polarization includes linear, circular and elliptical states. Linear angles are identified
      modulo \(\pi\), while the Stokes vector places pure states on the Poincaré sphere. Jones matrices act on
      amplitudes; their corresponding rotations act on Stokes vectors. An overall complex phase is invisible
      to an isolated intensity measurement but can become a relative phase in an interferometer.</p>
    <p>A quarter-wave plate is not an order-two inversion: two identical quarter-wave passages make a
      half-wave retardance, not generally the identity. A mirror may also change handedness conventions and
      propagation direction. Any comparison with a Möbius circuit must therefore name the optical operation,
      the coordinate convention and the measured observable.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap reveal">
  <div class="page-head tight">
    <p class="kicker">Five possible meanings of residue</p>
    <h2 id="t-residue-ledger">Where Something Could Survive</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="grid two">
    <article class="frame card"><h3>1 &middot; Topological holonomy <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></h3><p>A local frame is restored after two Möbius circuits, while the surface remains globally non-orientable. The &ldquo;residue&rdquo; is a property of the bundle or space, not a leftover material.</p></article>
    <article class="frame card"><h3>2 &middot; Geometric phase <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></h3><p>A cyclic polarization path can acquire a Pancharatnam&ndash;Berry phase determined by geometry on the Poincaré sphere. It is observed relative to a reference path, not as a failure of the final polarization state to return.</p></article>
    <article class="frame card"><h3>3 &middot; Hysteresis or dissipation <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></h3><p>A real optical element can heat, age, saturate or respond nonlinearly. The second operation then differs from the first. This is material memory, not ideal inversion algebra.</p></article>
    <article class="frame card"><h3>4 &middot; Decoherence or environment <span class="hist">&#9670;</span></h3><p>The selected degree of freedom may return while correlations leak into uncontrolled modes. A larger state description is required to locate the record.</p></article>
    <article class="frame card"><h3>5 &middot; TTI inherited residue <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></h3><p>TTI may propose a boundary variable \(r\) with its own update law, such as \((x,r)\mapsto(Px,r+f[x])\). That enlarged model can retain memory even when \(P^2x=x\), but the law and coupling must be derived and tested.</p></article>
    <article class="frame card illuminated"><h3>The forbidden shortcut</h3><p>&ldquo;It inverted, therefore it remembers&rdquo; is not a mechanism. Exact restoration in the declared state space is the null result; memory requires an independently measurable carrier.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">An experiment that can say no</p>
    <h2 id="t-experiment">Separate Return Error from Path Memory</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>Prepare a known polarization state and retain a coherent reference arm.</li>
      <li>Apply a calibrated order-two polarization transformation twice in the test arm.</li>
      <li>Use full polarimetry to measure final-state error, not intensity alone.</li>
      <li>Interfere test and reference arms to measure any relative geometric or dynamic phase.</li>
      <li>Repeat in reversed order and over wavelength, temperature and power to expose non-ideal memory.</li>
      <li>Declare the TTI residue model unsuccessful if every result is accounted for by calibrated optics, noise and environment.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>A positive phase measurement would establish an optical path effect. It would not by itself establish
      cosmic inheritance, consciousness, matter&ndash;antimatter conversion or a Möbius universe.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap reveal">
  <div class="page-head tight"><p class="kicker">Categories</p><h2 id="t-categories">What Kind of Claim Is Being Made?</h2></div>
  <div class="grid three">
    <div class="frame card"><h3>Topological</h3><p>Non-orientability and frame return after two circuits are mathematical.</p></div>
    <div class="frame card"><h3>Physical</h3><p>Jones matrices, retardance, polarimetry and geometric phase belong to optics.</p></div>
    <div class="frame card"><h3>Informational</h3><p>A surviving record requires a carrier and distinguishable states.</p></div>
    <div class="frame card"><h3>Philosophical</h3><p>Return-with-memory is a model of identity through change.</p></div>
    <div class="frame card"><h3>Spiritual</h3><p>Initiation and return may be meaningful analogies, not laboratory conclusions.</p></div>
    <div class="frame card"><h3>Cultural</h3><p>Möbius imagery has an artistic history separate from its mathematical definition.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--creed">
    <p class="kicker">Earned, chosen, refused</p>
    <h2 id="t-boundary">The Question Survives; the Shortcut Does Not</h2>
    <p><strong>Earned:</strong> exact order-two maps restore the modelled state, and closed optical paths can
      carry measurable relative phase. <strong>Chosen:</strong> asking whether a separately defined residue
      variable can connect those structures to TTI. <strong>Refused:</strong> treating any double inversion,
      any polarization change or any Möbius image as evidence for inherited physical memory.</p>
    <p>Read the parent account of <a href="/moebius/">the Möbius seam</a>, then compare
      <a href="/time-and-residue/">the one-residue proposal</a> and
      <a href="/out-of-phase/">matter and antimatter out of phase</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>
